# Simple English for MG Eye Foundation

All text a visitor reads (headings, buttons, paragraphs, FAQs, forms, alt text) must be **very easy English**. A person with little English should still understand it.

## Do

- Short sentences. One idea per sentence.
- Common words: eye, see, treat, scan, doctor, child, cost, come back.
- Say what happens in real life, not slogans.
- Use Hindi names only when the user already uses them (e.g. squint / bhengaapan if needed).

## Do not

- Fancy lines like “no guesswork”, “our strength”, “from darkness”, “duty”, “transaction”.
- Hard words: ethical, diagnostics, preventable, referral, facility (say hospital), consultation (say visit).
- Long stacked clauses.

## Example

Bad: “Deliver ethical cataract care with honest fees and no promise of cashless until it actually exists.”

Good: “We do cataract surgery. We tell you the cost first. Cashless is not available now.”
